### **Overall Detailed Summary of Workshop Sessions**

These sessions document a two-day workshop aimed at transitioning the **Controllership Finance team** from a manual, judgment-heavy reporting process to a cutting-edge, **AI-integrated web application**.

**Key Objectives and Strategic Vision:**
*   **Technological Modernization:** The team aims to move away from "decade-old" PowerBI dashboards to a custom **React-based web app**. This platform will utilize **Agentic AI** to provide automated summaries, "nudges" for collections, and predictive forecasting [1, 2].
*   **Phase 1 Deliverables:** The priority is to establish a **Business Requirement Document (BRD)** and a blueprint for automating the "as-is" process, specifically focusing on **Accounts Receivable (AR)** and **Cash Flow Forecasting** [3, 4].

**Current "As-Is" Process (Manual):**
*   **Reporting:** The team manually pulls three primary reports from **Oracle/Fusion**: Billed AR, Unbilled AR, and On-Account data [5, 6]. These reports are used to calculate a net position in local currencies (GBP, Euro, USD) and are converted to millions for reporting [7, 8].
*   **Hedging and Treasury:** A critical output of this process is a report provided to the **Banking/Treasury team** to facilitate **currency hedging**. Accurate forecasts are essential because inaccuracies lead to the company paying **higher bank premiums** [9, 10].
*   **Forecasting Accuracy:** The current manual process relies on "mental models" and historical judgment, yet it maintains a high accuracy rate of **97% to 98%** [2, 11].

**Strategic Levers for Improvement:**
*   **Days to Bill:** It currently takes an average of **18 days** to convert unbilled services into an invoice due to administrative delays, such as waiting for client Purchase Orders (POs) or draft invoice approvals [12, 13].
*   **Aging and DSO:** Invoices overdue by more than **90 days** are a "direct hit" to **Days Sales Outstanding (DSO)** [14]. The team uses a DSO gap formula (e.g., comparing a current 91-day DSO against a 58-day target) to determine necessary collection targets [15, 16].
*   **Bad Debt:** The company maintains a provision for bad debt of approximately **$3 million (about 1%)**, which covers disputes and bankruptcy cases (e.g., Chapter 11) [17, 18].

**Future AI Integration and Features:**
*   **Collection Prediction:** The AI will analyze **two years of historical data** to predict repayment behavior at the client and entity level [19, 20].
*   **Automated Follow-ups:** The app will feature a **"Customer Daily Risk"** component that prioritizes high-risk invoices and uses **Generative AI to draft follow-up emails** for account managers [21-23].
*   **Scenario Planning:** The tool will provide "optimistic" vs. "past trend" scenarios to help the team identify and bridge collection gaps [24, 25].
*   **Data Pipelines:** The project will automate data flows from Oracle to the dashboard to reduce manual workload and data drift [26, 27].

